<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <template id="report_sale_agreement">
        <t t-call="web.html_container">
            <t t-foreach="docs" t-as="order">
                <t t-call="web.external_layout">
                    <style>
                        .sgc-report {
                            font-family: "Helvetica", "Arial", sans-serif;
                            font-size: 12px;
                            color: #1f2937;
                            line-height: 1.45;
                        }
                        .sgc-header {
                            border: 1px solid #1e3a8a;
                            border-left: 6px solid #10b981;
                            background: #f8fafc;
                            padding: 12px 14px;
                            margin-bottom: 16px;
                        }
                        .sgc-kicker {
                            font-size: 10px;
                            letter-spacing: 0.08em;
                            text-transform: uppercase;
                            color: #1e3a8a;
                            font-weight: 700;
                        }
                        .sgc-title {
                            font-size: 22px;
                            color: #1e3a8a;
                            margin: 4px 0 0 0;
                            font-weight: 700;
                        }
                        .sgc-section-title {
                            margin: 16px 0 8px 0;
                            padding-bottom: 4px;
                            border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
                            color: #1e3a8a;
                            font-size: 14px;
                            font-weight: 700;
                        }
                        .sgc-table {
                            width: 100%;
                            border-collapse: collapse;
                            margin-bottom: 8px;
                        }
                        .sgc-table td {
                            border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
                            padding: 6px 8px;
                            vertical-align: top;
                        }
                        .sgc-table td:first-child {
                            width: 38%;
                            background: #f3f4f6;
                            font-weight: 700;
                            color: #111827;
                        }
                        .sgc-signature td {
                            min-height: 120px;
                        }
                    </style>
                    <div class="page sgc-report">
                        <div class="sgc-header">
                            <div class="sgc-kicker">SGC TECH AI - Commercial Agreement</div>
                            <h2 class="sgc-title">SaaS Subscription and Support Agreement</h2>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            This SaaS Subscription and Support Agreement is entered into on
                            <strong><span t-field="order.agreement_date"/></strong>
                            between <strong><span t-field="order.company_id.name"/></strong>
                            (the "Provider") and <strong><span t-field="order.partner_id.name"/></strong>
                            (the "Customer").
                        </p>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">1. Commercial Summary</h3>
                        <table class="sgc-table">
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Quotation / Order</strong></td>
                                <td><span t-field="order.name"/></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Customer Contact</strong></td>
                                <td><span t-field="order.agreement_contact_person"/> <t t-if="order.agreement_job_title">(<span t-field="order.agreement_job_title"/>)</t></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Authorized Users</strong></td>
                                <td><span t-field="order.num_users"/></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Service Term</strong></td>
                                <td><span t-esc="order._get_service_term_text()"/></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Monthly Subscription Fee</strong></td>
                                <td><span t-field="order.monthly_subscription_amount" t-options='{"widget": "monetary", "display_currency": order.currency_id}'/></td>
                            </tr>
                        </table>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">2. Services</h3>
                        <p>
                            Provider shall make available the hosted software services, user access, standard maintenance,
                            updates, and reasonable technical support for the modules and business functions purchased by Customer.
                        </p>
                        <p t-if="order.odoo_modules"><strong>Subscribed Modules:</strong></p>
                        <ul t-if="order.odoo_modules">
                            <li t-foreach="order._get_modules_list()" t-as="module_name"><span t-esc="module_name"/></li>
                        </ul>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">3. Subscription, Billing, and Renewal</h3>
                        <p>
                            Customer agrees to pay the monthly subscription fee stated above. Unless otherwise agreed in writing,
                            subscription charges are billed in advance on a recurring monthly basis and remain payable throughout
                            the active subscription term.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Any implementation, onboarding, or project fees reflected in the sales order remain payable in accordance
                            with the commercial terms of that order. Recurring subscription fees may be revised upon renewal or by
                            prior written notice where permitted by applicable law and the governing commercial documents.
                        </p>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">4. User Access and Acceptable Use</h3>
                        <p>
                            Customer may permit up to the agreed number of named or authorized users to access the service.
                            Customer is responsible for all activities performed through its accounts, for safeguarding credentials,
                            and for ensuring users do not misuse the platform, attempt unauthorized access, or infringe third-party rights.
                        </p>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">5. Support and Maintenance</h3>
                        <p>
                            Provider will use commercially reasonable efforts to maintain service availability, apply updates,
                            correct defects, and provide operational support during normal support coverage windows. Support does not
                            include custom development or third-party issues unless expressly included in the applicable order.
                        </p>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">6. Customer Responsibilities</h3>
                        <p>
                            Customer shall provide timely cooperation, accurate business information, designated points of contact,
                            and any licenses, approvals, or documents reasonably required for onboarding, configuration, compliance,
                            and ongoing service delivery.
                        </p>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">7. Data Protection and Confidentiality</h3>
                        <p>
                            Each party shall protect the other party's confidential information and use it only for purposes of this
                            Agreement. Customer retains ownership of its business data. Provider may process and host Customer data solely
                            for the purpose of delivering the subscribed services, subject to applicable law and Provider's security practices.
                        </p>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">8. Intellectual Property</h3>
                        <p>
                            Provider and its licensors retain all right, title, and interest in the software, platform, documentation,
                            updates, and related intellectual property. Customer receives a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable right
                            to use the subscribed services during the active subscription term.
                        </p>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">9. Suspension and Termination</h3>
                        <p>
                            Provider may suspend or terminate access for material breach, non-payment, security risk, or unlawful use,
                            following notice where commercially reasonable. Customer may terminate in accordance with the applicable order
                            or by written notice at the end of the current subscription term, subject to any minimum term commitments.
                        </p>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">10. Warranties and Liability</h3>
                        <p>
                            Provider warrants that the services will be provided in a professional and commercially reasonable manner.
                            Except as expressly stated, the services are provided on an "as available" basis. To the maximum extent permitted
                            by law, neither party shall be liable for indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages. Provider's total
                            aggregate liability arising out of this Agreement shall not exceed the fees paid by Customer for the three months
                            immediately preceding the event giving rise to the claim.
                        </p>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">11. General</h3>
                        <p>
                            This Agreement together with the related sales order constitutes the entire agreement between the parties for the
                            subscribed services. Any amendment must be in writing. If any provision is unenforceable, the remaining provisions
                            will continue in full force and effect.
                        </p>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">12. Signatures</h3>
                        <table class="sgc-table sgc-signature" style="margin-top: 16px;">
                            <tr>
                                <td style="width: 50%; vertical-align: top;">
                                    <strong>Customer</strong><br/>
                                    Name: <span t-field="order.client_signer_name"/><br/>
                                    Company: <span t-field="order.partner_id.name"/><br/>
                                    Date: <span t-field="order.client_sign_date"/>
                                </td>
                                <td style="width: 50%; vertical-align: top;">
                                    <strong>Provider</strong><br/>
                                    Name: <span t-field="order.provider_signer_name"/><br/>
                                    Company: <span t-field="order.company_id.name"/><br/>
                                    Date: <span t-field="order.provider_sign_date"/>
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </t>
            </t>
        </t>
    </template>

    <template id="report_sale_agreement_yearly">
        <t t-call="web.html_container">
            <t t-foreach="docs" t-as="agreement">
                <t t-call="web.external_layout">
                    <div class="page sgc-report">
                        <div class="sgc-header">
                            <div class="sgc-kicker">SGC TECH AI - Annual Renewal</div>
                            <h2 class="sgc-title">Annual SaaS Subscription Renewal Agreement</h2>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            This renewal agreement confirms the annual SaaS subscription arrangement between
                            <strong><span t-field="agreement.company_id.name"/></strong>
                            (the "Provider") and <strong><span t-field="agreement.partner_id.name"/></strong>
                            (the "Customer") for agreement year <strong><span t-field="agreement.agreement_year"/></strong>.
                        </p>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">1. Renewal Summary</h3>
                        <table class="sgc-table">
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Agreement Reference</strong></td>
                                <td><span t-field="agreement.name"/></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Agreement Date</strong></td>
                                <td><span t-field="agreement.agreement_date"/></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Customer Contact</strong></td>
                                <td><span t-field="agreement.agreement_contact_person"/> <t t-if="agreement.agreement_job_title">(<span t-field="agreement.agreement_job_title"/>)</t></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Authorized Users</strong></td>
                                <td><span t-field="agreement.num_users"/></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Service Term</strong></td>
                                <td><span t-esc="agreement._get_service_term_text()"/></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><strong>Monthly Subscription Fee</strong></td>
                                <td><span t-field="agreement.monthly_subscription_amount" t-options='{"widget": "monetary", "display_currency": agreement.currency_id}'/></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr t-if="agreement.sale_order_id">
                                <td><strong>Related Sales Order</strong></td>
                                <td><span t-field="agreement.sale_order_id.name"/></td>
                            </tr>
                        </table>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">2. Continued Subscription Services</h3>
                        <p>
                            Provider shall continue to provide hosted access to the subscribed software environment, platform maintenance,
                            updates, standard support, and operational continuity for the Customer's active deployment.
                        </p>
                        <p t-if="agreement.odoo_modules"><strong>Covered Modules:</strong></p>
                        <ul t-if="agreement.odoo_modules">
                            <li t-foreach="agreement._get_modules_list()" t-as="module_name"><span t-esc="module_name"/></li>
                        </ul>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">3. Fees and Payment Terms</h3>
                        <p>
                            Customer shall pay the monthly subscription fee stated above for the renewal term. Fees are billed monthly in advance,
                            unless another written billing arrangement applies. Late payment may result in suspension of services after reasonable notice.
                        </p>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">4. User Management</h3>
                        <p>
                            Customer is responsible for keeping its authorized user count accurate and ensuring only approved personnel have access.
                            Additional users, storage, modules, or service scope changes may require a commercial amendment.
                        </p>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">5. Support, Security, and Data Handling</h3>
                        <p>
                            Provider will continue commercially reasonable support, maintenance, and security administration for the hosted environment.
                            Customer remains responsible for the lawful use of the platform, the content it uploads, and internal user administration.
                        </p>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">6. Confidentiality, IP, and Liability</h3>
                        <p>
                            Confidentiality, intellectual property ownership, warranty limitations, and liability limitations remain governed by the main
                            commercial agreement, applicable order documents, and Provider policies, except where expressly modified in writing.
                        </p>

                        <h3 class="sgc-section-title">7. Renewal and Termination</h3>
                        <p>
                            This renewal continues for the stated annual cycle and renews subject to the commercial agreement between the parties.
                            Either party may elect not to renew or may terminate for material breach in accordance with the governing subscription terms.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </t>
            </t>
        </t>
    </template>
</odoo>
